From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:32:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845: add the CX power domain to camcc

The camera clock controller had no power domain, so its GDSCs had no
parent and nothing tied the camera clock rates to a CX corner. The
downstream camcc votes CX per source clock rate: BPS, IPE and IFE need
CX NOMINAL at 600 MHz and SVS_L1 at 480 MHz, and every camera clock needs
at least SVS. On mainline the ISP ran correctly only because another
voter happened to hold CX high.

Put camcc on CX, as GCC already is. Each GDSC then becomes a CX
subdomain, and a camera block whose OPP table has required-opps on
rpmhpd (attached to its GDSC) votes the CX corner its clock rate needs.
The vote passes through the GDSC unchanged, as UFS's does through
UFS_PHY_GDSC.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
index b1f6782a3a..2a2e24891c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
@@ -4604,6 +4604,7 @@ clock_camcc: clock-controller@ad00000 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
 			clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "bi_tcxo";
+			power-domains = <&rpmhpd SDM845_CX>;
 		};
 
 		mdss: display-subsystem@ae00000 {
